# PresenceDot — is this person here right now.
#
# A dot and nothing else. The name beside it is the caller's — `UserChip`,
# `PersonRow`, a message header — and a presence component that carried a name
# would be a second, worse identity line competing with the one already there.
#
# ── ONLINE IS A FACT ABOUT TIME, NOT A FLAG ─────────────────────────────────
#
# The caller passes a bool, and the bool it should pass is derived from a
# heartbeat: `now() - u.seenAt < 60`. A stored `online: bool` column is the
# version that breaks, and it breaks in the one way users notice — a browser that
# closes without saying goodbye leaves the flag true forever, so the list fills
# with people who are permanently "online" and the indicator stops meaning
# anything. A timestamp cannot lie about that; it just goes stale on its own.
#
#     use PresenceDot(asOf - u.seenAt < 60)
#
# `asOf` is an instant the caller supplies, for the reason live/timeago.fct sets
# out at length: a view cannot read the clock.
#
# `title` is not a parameter because this library has `ui/Tooltip` for the case
# where the dot needs words, and two ways to attach a label to one mark is one
# too many.
app FacetLive:
    css:
        [data-fa-mount] .x-presence { display: inline-block; width: 8px; height: 8px;
                       border-radius: 9999px; flex: none;
                       /* the ring separates the dot from whatever it sits on,
                          including an avatar it may overlap */
                       box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px var(--fa-bg); }
        [data-fa-mount] .x-presence-on { background: #00ba7c; }
        [data-fa-mount] .x-presence-off { background: var(--fa-muted); opacity: .5; }
    component PresenceDot(online: bool):
        if online:
            box class "x-presence x-presence-on"
        if !online:
            box class "x-presence x-presence-off"
